## Goal

Move the golden replay's pure half into a new module, `jackioh_engine::testkit::golden`. That covers `Mismatch` and its report, the canonical texts, `check_snapshot`, replaying one trace line, and the hotseat fold with its one `HOTSEAT_HASH`. Then `crates/engine/tests/golden.rs` and `crates/tools/src/golden.rs` (`golden check`) both call it. Each caller keeps its own I/O: it writes its own diff file and prints its own report. Traces, hashes, report wording and `GOLDEN_SHARDS` stay as they are, and no `#[allow]` is added. Two tests show that a doctored hash makes both callers name the same seed, step, hash and action. I prototyped it in a scratch copy, and every check below passed.

## Files to touch

| Path | new/change | What |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `crates/engine/src/testkit/golden.rs` | new | `FORMAT_VERSION`, `HOTSEAT`, `HOTSEAT_HASH`, `Mismatch` (+`diff_file`, `report`), `seed_number`, `hashed_state_text`, `view_texts`, `events_text`, `legal_text`, private `recorded` and `check_snapshot`, `replay_game`, `check_hotseat` |
| `crates/engine/src/testkit/mod.rs` | change | `pub mod golden;` and one header paragraph; no glob re-export |
| `crates/engine/Cargo.toml` | change | `required-features = ["testkit"]` on `[[test]] golden` |
| `crates/engine/tests/golden.rs` | change | drop the duplicates; `write_diff(&mut Mismatch)`; thin `replay_line`; hotseat uses `HOTSEAT`/`HOTSEAT_HASH`/`check_hotseat`; new test `a_doctored_trace` |
| `crates/tools/src/golden.rs` | change | drop the duplicates, import from `testkit::golden`; `write_diff(&mut Mismatch)`; `run_check` writes the diff |
| `crates/tools/tests/golden.rs` | new | `golden check` on a doctored copy of trace 1 |
| `crates/engine/README.md` | change | Features row `testkit`, Tests row `golden` |
| `crates/tools/README.md` | change | row `golden check`, `golden bless` |

Do not touch: `crates/tools/tests/luau.rs`, `crates/tools/src/{classify,luau,replay,think}.rs`, `crates/engine/tests/golden/*` (no trace or fixture edit), `spec/`, `docs/`, `.github/`, `scripts/`, any `clippy.toml`. Governing text: SURFACE §13.3 (`docs/v0.3.0/SURFACE.md`), CLAUDE.md rule 4 (the engine's `clippy.toml` bans file I/O in its library, testkit included). No ruling is added or cited anew. R781000's test stays in `crates/engine/tests/golden.rs` (its `proven_in`).

